From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Layer permissions: status cell, popover and offer

The status cell is the first column of the shelf's status slots and spans
both rows: one or two overlaying apps' icons ringed in the LumaUI overlay
violet, or the most recent icon and "+N". It shows while an overlay
surface is on screen and leaves 2 s after the last one goes; while an app
holds the keyboard through a layer surface it shows that app with a
keyboard badge. Hovering shows the shelf tooltip. A click opens a 312 px
shell pop listing each app with what it shows, for how long, and Stop
(org.projectluma.LayerShell1.Stop: unmapped for the session, the grant
kept), and Overlay settings (Settings, Apps, Display over other apps). A
click never stops anything by itself. On a phone the cell sits in the
status bar's right group and the list is a bottom drawer; on a TV the cell
sits in the top bar's status group and the list is a quick-panel page at
TV scale (48 px icons) with the focus on the first Stop.

The offer is the standard notification banner from the app's own source:
the app's name as the source line, its icon as the tile with the Settings
icon as a badge only the Shell can set, the capability's name as the
title, the question as the body, "now", and Allow and Not now as ordinary
content-width actions with neither a default. The banner sizes to its
content. Dismissing it counts as Not now. On a TV, where the notification
lip is hidden, it is that banner at TV scale (x1.5) at the top right, the
question wrapping, with the remote's focus on Not now.

The name tag on a faded overlay draws its violet ring outside the 26 px
pill, as designed; an app whose overlays fade gets one tag, on its
largest surface.

Every app icon here (the cell, the rows, the name tag, the TV toast's tile
and badge, the offer's Settings badge) is drawn through syncAppIconPlate
(0389), its plate filling a masked clip.

Design: design-center 4933aaa, mockups/overlay-perms.
